  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Response To Mulitaka Landslide-Affected Populations In Enga Province, Papua New Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Mount Mungalo landslide is the latest in a series of deadly landslides to have occurred in the Highlands Provinces of Papua New Guinea in recent months after fourteen people were buried alive in Simbu province in April 2024, and at least 21 people died in three separate landslides across the country in mid-March 2024. On 24 May 2024, a significant landslide occurred in Maip Muritaka Rural Local-Level Government in Lagaip-Porgera district, leading to extensive damage and fatalities. The International Organization for Migration is contributing towards mitigating the impacts of the Mulitaka Landslide in Enga Province through the delivery of lifesaving assistance to affected populations. In collaboration with the Provincial Disaster Coordination Office and the Disaster Management Team, IOM is expanding its services to meet the shelter, food and health/mental health and psychosocial needs of communities affected by landslides. The assistance is helping to facilitate the return of internally displaced persons, where feasible and safe, and improving living conditions in landslide-affected villages.</narrative>
  </description>
